    "recommendations": "• Install a reflective address marker at the driveway entrance to help responders locate the property quickly from the road.\n• Trim trees and shrubs along the access drive so emergency vehicles can travel its full length without obstruction.\n• Keep the access drive clear of parked vehicles, equipment, and debris so emergency vehicles can reach the main residence and detached structure without delay.\n• Mark the driveway entrance width visibly so responders know whether large vehicles can enter before committing to the drive.\n• Cut back dense vegetation along the sides of the access drive to give responders clear sightlines to both structures as they approach.\n• Post a property layout diagram near the driveway entrance showing the location of the main residence, detached structure, and pool area so arriving responders can orient quickly.\n• Create a clear walking path between the main residence and the detached structure so responders can move between the two buildings on foot without pushing through vegetation.\n• Keep a gate or opening in any fencing around the pool area accessible and unlockable from the outside so responders can reach or work around the pool without delay.\n• Mark the pool area visibly from the access drive so responders are aware of its location during night or low-visibility operations.\n• Thin dense vegetation at the rear of the property to give responders at least one usable path to the back of the main residence.\n•"
