    "recommendations": "• Trim back shrubs and grass that are growing directly against the exterior walls of the structure.\n• Thin the tree cluster near the structure to open up space between the trees and the building.\n• Remove or cut back mixed vegetation growing close to the structure on all sides.\n• Clear grass and low shrubs from the ground beneath scattered trees near the structure.\n• Cut grass around the structure short and keep it mowed regularly.\n• Trim overhanging branches from scattered trees along the driveway to keep the travel lane open.\n• Clear shrubs and tall grass growing along the edges of the driveway for its full length.\n• Remove any dead or dry plant material from shrubs and grass patches near the structure.\n• Separate shrub groupings near the structure so there are clear gaps between them and the building.\n• Keep the driveway surface and shoulders clear of fallen branches and debris to allow vehicle access.\n• Thin shrubs growing along the driveway so they do not narrow or block the travel lane.\n• Cut back vegetation on both sides of the driveway entrance to maintain clear sightlines for incoming vehicles."
